And I realise that number might not mean much to you but this is a number so unimaginably tiny

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:30.200
that if we were to apply our tennis ball scale, our penny would be bigger than our entire galaxy.

00:06:30.400 --> 00:06:34.120
Except, to say that is an understatement would be an understatement!

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:37.980
The entire observable universe is 93 billion lightyears wide,

00:06:37.980 --> 00:06:41.880
and our Planck penny would be 90,000 times bigger than that!

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:45.000
Let me show you exactly how big that is.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:51.320
If we were to confine the entire observable universe into just a single pixel on a 4K TV,

00:06:51.880 --> 00:06:55.040
you would need over 800 TVs!

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:58.060
Just to see our entire penny.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:01.760
That is how small the Planck length is.

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:04.400
Infinity goes both ways.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:08.820
Our universe is inconceivably large and yet, it is also so inconceivably small.

00:07:08.820 --> 00:07:13.700
It really feels like a fractal, with no end in how big or small it can possibly be.

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:16.520
Our only limit is how far we can see.

00:07:17.260 --> 00:07:18.660
Thanks for watching.

